 worrying that only 12 percent feel  that they have been empowered that's  something that we need to talk about  again um thankfully when this open  letter came out the education minister  reached out to us and said he wants to  have that conversation so that puts us  in a real great position where we can  actually have that dialogue but the  biggest thing for me as i said earlier  with solutions is i've been to schools  where it's been enacted and enabled on  it doesn't cost anything else it's  already in the budget because i did ask  these schools are you having to find  additional money they said no it's  already in there  that was one thing but the biggest thing  is there is groups out there now  actively teaching uh teachers the  dialogue the right way to deliver uh  because as we know it's a really uh  difficult and tough subject so um we  want to be able to to speak  but also give teachers that  self-assurance that what you're speaking  will not get you sucked you know if you  say something wrong and admit to that  you know with the intention of doing  something right you won't get sacked you  won't be  out of the role because i think that is  where a lot of the problems come now  people are very worried about what they  say and how they say it so they're just  saying nothing can we ignore the uh the  situation  now the welsh government of course has  taken the lead here what's the noises  that you're hearing when you're speaking  to  the government here in england  um as i say we already reached out last  night and and within an hour we got a  response which was something that uh  caught us off quite hard if we're being  totally honest we anticipated that being  having to get a more  social and as much presence as possible  to generate that noise for to hear back  so what we're hearing now is that there  is um actually  some evidence that they want to reach  out they want to  listen and see what the solutions are so  it's on us now to get everybody behind  it with the help of yourselves giving me  a platform to talk where we can we've  created a hashtag this allows people to  talk about their experiences of school  and we're hoping to do something  similarly to the metoo movement where  people can have their experiences on  there and we can talk and create a  conversation that we can then put to  government as well that it's not just  troy and this survey it's lots and lots  of people's uh opinions  their their school in education and  their feelings and we can talk and  hopefully get to a positive uh solution  for this  absolutely and try hopefully you can  keep us up to date with um how you get  on thank you very much indeed troy  deeney there speaking to us
 

